#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bookkeeping in PLAN.md, without hand edits (WORKFLOW.md §3, §5.2, §10).

Each command changes PLAN.md in one place, checks the result with scripts/check-plan, and writes
it. Add --commit to commit it (one commit, a standard message). Add --dry-run to print the diff
and change nothing. The ownership rules of WORKFLOW.md §3 apply: coordinator commands run only
on main, slice owner commands only on the branch of that slice.

PLAN.md exists only while a requirement is in progress. With no PLAN.md, every command except
`new` stops and says so. Every write redraws §2 Map from the Needs fields and lints the format
(scripts/lib/plangen.py) before check-plan.

Read-only (anywhere):
  plan show <ID>                       the §0 row and the slice section
  plan title [--milestone M1]          the coordinator status title, counted from §0
  plan lint                            check the format of PLAN.md and the files in plan/ (exit 1)
  plan dag --json                      write the graph of plan/plan.json (nodes, edges, order) to
        stdout; a cycle, an unknown need or a schema error makes it fail (no PLAN.md needed)
  plan passed <ID> [--json] [--base REF]   passed of each item of <ID>, derived from the
        verifier results for the head commit of its branch (scripts/lib/plandata.py); results
        for an older commit are stale and count for nothing. The branch and the items come from
        plan/ as committed at REF (default HEAD), never from an uncommitted edit

Verifier (not the slice owner; WORKFLOW.md §10):
  plan verify <ID> [--base REF]        check out the head commit of the branch of <ID> (from
        plan/plan.json as committed at REF, default HEAD) clean, run the `cmd:` evidence of each
        item there (and check `commit:` pointers), and store the commands and exit codes as a
        git note on that commit. The only way to make results: no command takes them from
        outside. A `cmd:` is a repo-relative executable file of the commit, with no symlink in
        its path. Logs: /tmp/dshm-verify/

Merge step (the coordinator, or the merge node of the Workflow):
  plan merge <ID> --into <branch> [--allow-changed-evidence PATH] [--dry-run]
        merge the branch of <ID> into <branch> only if the checks pass on the merge commit.
        It always runs the copy of these tools committed at the tip of <branch> (it starts that
        copy from a clean checkout when the running copy differs), takes the branch and the
        items from plan/ as committed there (the slice branch may only add evidence), makes the
        merge commit in a clean checkout, runs the evidence on it, stores the results on the
        merge commit, and then moves <branch> to it. It reads no report and no earlier results.
        An evidence file (a `cmd:` executable, a file argument, or a file that such a script
        names) that the target has and the branch changes or deletes stops the merge: a reviewer
        or the user must look at it. After that, the coordinator passes
        --allow-changed-evidence <path> (repeatable); the merge commit message records it. New
        evidence files of the branch are listed as "new evidence, judged by the reviewer".
        Prints a JSON summary; exit 0 = merged (--dry-run: passed), 1 = not

Coordinator (on main):
  plan new "<title>"                   start the plan of a requirement the user has set, from
        scripts/lib/plan-template.md (refused if PLAN.md exists). Title: "M2 · Push and replies"
  plan add tracer|spike|slice "<name>" --why T --cuts T --done "[auto] …" [--done …]
        [--needs "T0, X1"] [--demo T] [--not T]
        add a section in the format: the next ID (T0, X1, S1, …), a §0 row (todo), the fields in
        order. A slice needs the first tracer unless --needs says otherwise. A value with a
        newline is written under the field name (bullets); --cuts - reads stdin
  plan add exit "<item>"               add a [human] item to §6 Exit
  plan row <ID> <status> [--branch T] [--next T]       change the §0 row (Updated = today)
  plan log "<title>" [--body T|-]                       add a §8 entry (- = body from stdin)
  plan pending <slice> <kind> "<item>" [--branch B] [--commit-ref C]   add a §9 row
  plan fix "<name>" --bug "<what the user saw>" [--needs ID]
        a bug that the user reported: add a fix slice (next S number, a §0 row, a section);
        then `plan assign` and start a session for it. The coordinator does not fix code.
  plan assign <ID> --branch B [--worktree P] [--from C] [--decisions N] [--note T]
        give the slice its resources (scripts/slice-env), set §0 to doing, add the §8 entry
  plan merged <ID> <merge-commit> [--note T] [--keep]
        after a merge: check PLAN.md of the merge commit against its first parent (§10, condition
        3); set §0 to review (open [human] items) or done; add §9 rows for the open [human]
        items and for the provisional D entries that the merge added; add the §8 entry with the
        review result from /tmp/dshm-review. Then the cleanup below; --keep skips it
  plan cleanup <ID>
        remove what a merged slice left on the Mac, and print each thing: the simulator dshm-<ID>;
        /tmp/dshm-<id> and /tmp/dshm-<id>-*; each worktree and branch of the slice whose HEAD is
        an ancestor of the merge commit (`cleanup`: of main) and that has no uncommitted or
        untracked file (`git worktree remove`, `git branch -d`, never forced); its DSHM_HOME if it
        is inside ~/.dshm/. A simulator that a running demo owns (/tmp/dshm-guard) and a /tmp path
        that a running process names stay. It prints what it leaves, and why. Only for a slice
        that is review or done. With DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY=1 or --dry-run it prints what it would
        remove and removes nothing

Slice owner (on the slice branch):
  plan tick <ID> "<part of the item>" --evidence "test:… · cmd:…"   tick one [auto]/[ui] item
  plan slice-log <ID> "<title>" [--body T|-]                         add a dated Log entry
  plan slice-status <ID> <status>                                    the Status field

Exit 0 = OK, 1 = refused or check failed, 2 = usage.
"""

import argparse
import difflib
import glob
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "lib"))
import dshm  # noqa: E402
import plandata  # noqa: E402
import plangen  # noqa: E402

PlanError = dshm.PlanError
TRAILER = "\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"


class Plan:
    def __init__(self, root):
        self.root = root
        self.path = root / "PLAN.md"
        self.exists = self.path.exists()
        self.before = self.path.read_text() if self.exists else ""
        self.lines = dshm.split_lines(self.before) if self.exists else []
        self.extra_files = []      # other files to commit with PLAN.md

    # -- write ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    def text(self):
        return "\n".join(self.lines)

    def save(self, args, message):
        plangen.redraw_map(self.lines)
        errors = plangen.lint(self.lines)
        if errors:
            raise PlanError("the plan format is broken (scripts/lib/plangen.py):\n  " + "\n  ".join(errors))
        after = self.text()
        if after == self.before:
            print("plan: no change")
            return 0
        if args.dry_run:
            sys.stdout.writelines(difflib.unified_diff(
                self.before.splitlines(True), after.splitlines(True), "PLAN.md", "PLAN.md (new)"))
            return 0
        check(self.root, self.before, after)
        self.path.write_text(after)
        print(f"plan: PLAN.md changed ({message})")
        if args.commit:
            files = ["PLAN.md", *self.extra_files]
            dshm.git("add", "--", *files, cwd=self.root)
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "commit", "-q", "-m", message + TRAILER, "--", *files],
                               cwd=self.root, capture_output=True, text=True)
            if r.returncode != 0:
                raise PlanError(f"git commit failed:\n{r.stdout}{r.stderr}")
            print(f"plan: committed {dshm.git('rev-parse', '--short', 'HEAD', cwd=self.root)} {message}")
        return 0

    # -- §0 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    def row(self, sid):
        for i, r in dshm.status_table(self.lines):
            if r["id"] == sid:
                return i, r
        raise PlanError(f"{sid} has no row in §0 (adding a row is a plan change for the user)")

    def set_row(self, sid, status=None, branch=None, nxt=None):
        i, r = self.row(sid)
        if status:
            if status not in dshm.STATUSES:
                raise PlanError(f"status must be one of {', '.join(dshm.STATUSES)}")
            r["status"] = status
        if branch is not None:
            r["branch"] = branch
        if nxt is not None:
            r["next"] = nxt
        r["updated"] = dshm.today()
        self.lines[i] = dshm.format_row([r["id"], r["status"], r["branch"], r["updated"], r["next"]])

    # -- §8 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    def add_log(self, title, body=""):
        entry = format_entry(title, body)
        _, e = dshm.section_bounds(self.lines, "## 8. Plan log")
        while e > 0 and self.lines[e - 1].strip() == "":
            e -= 1
        self.lines[e:e] = ["", *entry]
        # one blank line before the next heading
        _, e2 = dshm.section_bounds(self.lines, "## 8. Plan log")
        if self.lines[e2 - 1].strip() != "":
            self.lines.insert(e2, "")

    # -- §9 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    def add_pending(self, sid, kind, item, branch="`main`", ref="—"):
        s, e = dshm.section_bounds(self.lines, "## 9. Pending user confirmation")
        last, numbers = None, []
        for i in range(s, e):
            cells = dshm.table_cells(self.lines[i])
            if cells and cells[0].isdigit():
                last = i
                numbers.append(int(cells[0]))
        if last is None:   # an empty table: the first row goes under the |---| line
            last = next((i for i in range(s, e) if self.lines[i].startswith("|---")), None)
            if last is None:
                raise PlanError("§9 has no table to add to")
            # Keep the numbers unique: §8 entries name the rows that left ("§9 rows 63, 64").
            for m in re.finditer(r"§9 rows? (\d+(?:(?:, | and |–|-)\d+)*)", self.text()):
                numbers += [int(x) for x in re.findall(r"\d+", m.group(1))]
        n = max(numbers, default=0) + 1
        self.lines.insert(last + 1, dshm.format_row([str(n), sid, kind, item.replace("|", "\\|"), branch, ref]))
        return n


def format_entry(title, body):
    title = title.strip().rstrip(".")
    body_lines = [l.rstrip() for l in (body or "").strip("\n").split("\n")] if body and body.strip() else []
    head = f"- **{dshm.today()} · {title}.**"
    if body_lines and not body_lines[0].lstrip().startswith("- "):
        head += " " + body_lines.pop(0).strip()
    rest = [("  " + l if l and not l.startswith("  ") else l) for l in body_lines]
    return [head, *rest]


def check(root, before, after):
    """scripts/check-plan on this one edit (--agent: no [human] tick, no pre-ticked new item)."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
        b, a = Path(d, "base.md"), Path(d, "new.md")
        b.write_text(before)
        a.write_text(after)
        r = subprocess.run([str(root / "scripts/check-plan"), "--base", str(b), "--new", str(a), "--agent"],
                           cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise PlanError("scripts/check-plan refused the change:\n" + r.stdout + r.stderr)


def read_body(value):
    if value == "-":
        return sys.stdin.read()
    return value or ""


def need_main():
    b = dshm.branch()
    if b != "main":
        raise PlanError(f"this command is for the coordinator, on main (now on {b}); WORKFLOW.md §3")


def need_slice_branch(sid):
    b = dshm.branch()
    key = sid.lower()
    if b == "main" or not re.search(rf"(^|/){re.escape(key)}(-|$)", b):
        raise PlanError(f"this command is for the owner of {sid}, on its branch (now on {b}); WORKFLOW.md §3")


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- commands

def cmd_show(p, a):
    _, r = p.row(a.id)
    print(dshm.format_row([r["id"], r["status"], r["branch"], r["updated"], r["next"]]))
    print()
    s, e = dshm.slice_bounds(p.lines, a.id)
    print("\n".join(p.lines[s:e]).rstrip())
    return 0


def title_from(lines, milestone):
    marks = {"done": "✅", "review": "👀", "doing": "🔨", "blocked": "⏸"}
    count = {k: 0 for k in marks}
    for _, r in dshm.status_table(lines):
        if r["status"] in count:
            count[r["status"]] += 1
    return f"🎛 Coordinator · {milestone} · " + " ".join(f"{marks[k]}{count[k]}" for k in marks)


def cmd_title(p, a):
    print(title_from(p.lines, a.milestone or plangen.plan_title(p.lines)))
    return 0


def cmd_lint(p, a):
    errors = plangen.lint(p.lines) + plandata.tree_errors(plandata.worktree_files(p.root))
    for e in errors:
        print(f"plan lint: {e}")
    if not errors:
        print("plan lint: OK")
    return 1 if errors else 0


def cmd_dag(p, a):
    try:
        g = plandata.dag(plandata.load_plan(p.root))
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(g, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    else:
        for sid in g["order"]:
            n = next(n for n in g["nodes"] if n["id"] == sid)
            print(f"{sid}  needs {', '.join(n['needs']) or '—'}  {n['title']}")
    return 0


def cmd_passed(p, a):
    try:
        d = plandata.derive(p.root, a.id, a.base)
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(d, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    head = d["head"][:12] if d["head"] else "no commit"
    who = f"verified by {d['verifier']} at {d['verified_at']}" if d["verifier"] else "no verifier results for this commit"
    print(f"{d['id']} · {d['branch'] or 'no branch'} @ {head} · {who}")
    if d["stale"]:
        print(f"  stale: results for {d['stale'][:12]} do not count for {head}")
    for it in d["items"]:
        mark = "x" if it["passed"] else " "
        runs = " · ".join(f"{r['cmd']} → {r['exit']}" for r in it["runs"])
        print(f"  [{mark}] [{it['tier']}] {it['text']}" + (f" — {runs}" if runs else ""))
    print(f"passed: {str(d['passed']).lower()}")
    return 0


def cmd_verify(p, a):
    try:
        res = plandata.verify(p.root, a.id, a.base, say=lambda m: print(f"plan: {m}", flush=True, file=sys.stderr))
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    ok = sum(1 for r in res["items"] if plandata.item_passed(r))
    print(f"plan: verified {a.id} at {res['commit'][:12]}: {ok} of {len(res['items'])} items passed "
          f"({plandata.NOTES_REF})")
    return 0


def cmd_merge(p, a):
    root, say = p.root, (lambda m: print(f"plan: {m}", flush=True, file=sys.stderr))
    base = dshm.git("rev-parse", "-q", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{a.into}^{{commit}}", cwd=root, check=False)
    if not base:
        raise PlanError(f"no branch {a.into}")
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
    if not plandata.same_as(root, base, here):
        # Not the copy of the tools at the tip of the target: run that copy instead.
        say(f"running the merge tools of {a.into} at {base[:12]}")
        with plandata.Checkout(root, base, f"merge-tools-{a.id.lower()}") as wt:
            argv = [sys.executable, str(wt / "scripts/plan"), "merge", a.id, "--into", a.into]
            argv += [x for f in a.allow for x in ("--allow-changed-evidence", f)]
            return subprocess.run(argv + (["--dry-run"] if a.dry_run else []), cwd=wt).returncode
    try:
        res = plandata.merge(root, a.id, a.into, dry=a.dry_run, allow=a.allow, say=say)
    except plandata.DataError as e:
        raise PlanError(str(e))
    print(json.dumps(res, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    for f in res["new_evidence"]:
        say(f"new evidence, judged by the reviewer: {f}")
    for f in res["allowed_changed_evidence"]:
        say(f"changed evidence allowed by --allow-changed-evidence: {f}")
    ok = res["passed"] if a.dry_run else res["merged"]
    say(("passed" if a.dry_run else f"merged {a.id} into {a.into} as {res['merge'][:12]}") if ok
        else f"not merged: the checks failed on the merge commit {res['merge'][:12]}")
    return 0 if ok else 1


def cmd_new(p, a):
    """Start the plan of a requirement that the user has set (WORKFLOW.md §3.1)."""
    need_main()
    if p.exists:
        raise PlanError("PLAN.md exists: one requirement at a time. The user deletes PLAN.md when "
                        "its exit passes; then start the next one")
    p.lines = dshm.split_lines(plangen.new_plan(a.title))
    p.extra_files = []
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN: start {plangen.plan_title(p.lines)}")


def cmd_add(p, a):
    need_main()
    if a.kind == "exit":
        plangen.add_exit(p.lines, a.name)
        return p.save(a, "PLAN §6: exit item")
    needs = None if a.needs is None else plangen.ID_RE.findall(a.needs)
    sid = plangen.add(p.lines, a.kind, a.name, needs, read_body(a.why), read_body(a.cuts),
                      read_body(a.demo), a.done or [], read_body(a.not_))
    print(f"plan: new {a.kind} {sid}")
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN: add {sid} ({a.name.strip()})")


def cmd_row(p, a):
    need_main()
    p.set_row(a.id, a.status, a.branch, a.next)
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN: {a.id} {a.status}")


def cmd_log(p, a):
    need_main()
    p.add_log(a.title, read_body(a.body))
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN §8: {a.title.strip().rstrip('.')}")


def cmd_fix(p, a):
    """A bug that the user reported becomes a fix slice: a §0 row and a section (WORKFLOW.md §5.2)."""
    need_main()
    name, bug = a.name.strip().rstrip("."), " ".join(a.bug.split()).rstrip(".")
    sid = plangen.add(
        p.lines, "slice", f"Fix: {name}", plangen.ID_RE.findall(a.needs or ""),
        why=f"The user reported a bug on {dshm.today()}: {bug}.",
        cuts="Find the cause. Fix it. Add a test that fails without the fix.",
        done=["[auto] A test reproduces the reported bug and passes with the fix",
              "[human] The user no longer sees the bug"],
        not_="Other changes. Report other bugs to the coordinator as new fix slices.",
        nxt=f"Fix: {name}; start a fix session")
    print(f"plan: new fix slice {sid}")
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN: {sid} fix slice ({name})")


def cmd_pending(p, a):
    need_main()
    n = p.add_pending(a.slice, a.kind, a.item, f"`{a.branch}`", f"`{a.commit_ref}`" if a.commit_ref else "—")
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN §9: row {n} ({a.slice} {a.kind})")


def cmd_assign(p, a):
    need_main()
    sys.path.insert(0, str(p.root / "scripts"))
    import importlib.machinery
    import importlib.util
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("slice_env", str(p.root / "scripts/slice-env"))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("slice_env", loader)
    se = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(se)
    if a.dry_run:
        raise PlanError("assign has no --dry-run (it writes the registry); use scripts/slice-env --list")
    row, new = se.assign(a.id, a.branch, a.decisions, p.root)
    p.extra_files.append(dshm.REGISTRY)
    p.set_row(a.id, "doing", f"`{a.branch}`", "Slice owner builds (§8)")
    where = f", worktree `{a.worktree}`" if a.worktree else ""
    base = f" (from `{a.from_commit}`)" if a.from_commit else ""
    body = (f"Branch `{a.branch}`{where}{base}, simulator `{row['sim']}`, DSHM_HOME `{row['home']}`, "
            f"bridge {row['bridge']}, web {row['web']}; second host {row['bridge2']}/{row['web2']}. "
            f"Decision numbers {row['decisions'].replace('-', '–')}. "
            f"`eval \"$(scripts/slice-env {a.id})\"` exports them.")
    if not new:
        body += " Same resources as before."
    if a.note:
        body += " " + a.note.strip()
    p.add_log(f"{a.id} assigned", body)
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN: assign {a.id}")


def review_line(sid, short):
    files = sorted(glob.glob(f"{os.environ.get('DSHM_REVIEW_DIR', '/tmp/dshm-review')}/{sid}-*.txt"),
                   key=os.path.getmtime)
    if not files:
        return None
    f = files[-1]
    text = Path(f).read_text()
    result = "PASS" if "RESULT: PASS" in text else "FAIL" if "RESULT: FAIL" in text else "?"
    flaky = " (flaky parts listed there)" if "flaky" in text else ", no flaky part"
    commit = Path(f).stem.split("-", 1)[1]
    return f"`scripts/review {sid}` at `{commit}`: `RESULT: {result}`{flaky} (`{f}`)."


def cmd_merged(p, a):
    need_main()
    root = p.root
    full = dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", f"{a.merge_commit}^{{commit}}", cwd=root)
    short = full[:7]
    parents = dshm.git("rev-list", "--parents", "-n", "1", full, cwd=root).split()[1:]
    if len(parents) < 2:
        raise PlanError(f"{short} is not a merge commit")
    # §10, condition 3: the merge commit skipped pre-commit; check its PLAN.md against parent 1.
    check(root, dshm.git("show", f"{parents[0]}:PLAN.md", cwd=root), dshm.git("show", f"{full}:PLAN.md", cwd=root))

    open_human = [m.group("desc").strip() for _, m in dshm.items(p.lines, a.id)
                  if m.group("tier") == "human" and m.group("box") == " "]
    old = dshm.decision_rows(dshm.git("show", f"{parents[0]}:ARCHITECTURE.md", cwd=root))
    new = dshm.decision_rows(dshm.git("show", f"{full}:ARCHITECTURE.md", cwd=root))
    added = [(n, new[n]) for n in sorted(new) if n not in old and "provisional" in new[n].lower()]
    _, r = p.row(a.id)
    branch = r["branch"] if r["branch"].startswith("`claude/") or r["branch"].startswith("`codex/") else "—"

    rows = []
    for n, line in added:
        m = re.search(r"\*\*(.+?)\*\*", line)
        summary = m.group(1).rstrip(".") if m else "see ARCHITECTURE.md"
        rows.append(p.add_pending(a.id, "decision", f"ARCHITECTURE D{n}, *provisional*: {summary}",
                                  branch, f"merged `{short}`"))
    for desc in open_human:
        rows.append(p.add_pending(a.id, "`[human]`", desc, "`main`", f"`{short}`"))

    ds = ", ".join(f"D{n}" for n, _ in added)
    if open_human:
        status = "review"
        nxt = f"User accepts {len(open_human)} `[human]` item{'s' if len(open_human) > 1 else ''} (§9)"
    else:
        status = "done"
        nxt = f"— (provisional {ds} in §9)" if ds else "—"
    p.set_row(a.id, status, f"merged `{short}`", nxt)

    parts = [f"Merged as `{short}`; `scripts/check-plan` on the merge commit passed."]
    rl = review_line(a.id, short)
    if rl:
        parts.append(rl)
    if open_human:
        parts.append(f"{len(open_human)} open `[human]` item{'s' if len(open_human) > 1 else ''}, so {a.id} is `review`.")
    else:
        parts.append(f"No open `[human]` items, so {a.id} is `done`.")
    if rows:
        parts.append(f"§9 rows {', '.join(map(str, rows))}" + (f" ({ds})." if ds else "."))
    if a.note:
        parts.append(a.note.strip())
    p.add_log(f"{a.id} merged", " ".join(parts))
    rc = p.save(a, f"PLAN: {a.id} {status}" + (f"; {ds} to §9" if ds else ""))
    if rc == 0 and not a.keep:
        cleanup(root, a.id, full, cleanup_dry(a))
    return rc


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- cleanup
# After a merge, remove what the slice left on the Mac (WORKFLOW.md §10). Each destructive call
# goes through destroy(): with DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY=1 (or --dry-run) it prints and deletes nothing.

def cleanup_dry(a):
    return bool(getattr(a, "dry_run", False)) or os.environ.get("DSHM_CLEANUP_DRY") == "1"


def destroy(dry, what, *steps):
    """Run steps (argv lists, or ("rm", path)) to remove <what>. Returns True when removed."""
    if dry:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: would remove {what}")
        return True
    for step in steps:
        try:
            if step[0] == "rm":
                path = Path(step[1])
                if path.is_symlink() or path.is_file():
                    path.unlink()
                elif path.is_dir():
                    shutil.rmtree(path)
                continue
            check = step[0] != "-"          # "-" prefix: a failure does not matter (shutdown)
            argv = step[1:] if not check else step
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True)
            if check and r.returncode != 0:
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left {what}: {' '.join(argv)} failed: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()}")
                return False
        except OSError as e:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left {what}: {e}")
            return False
    print(f"plan: cleanup: removed {what}")
    return True


def cleanup(root, sid, target, dry):
    """Remove the simulator, /tmp dirs, worktrees, branches and DSHM_HOME of slice <sid>.
    A worktree or branch goes only when its HEAD is an ancestor of <target> and it is clean."""
    reg = [r for r in dshm.parse_registry((root / dshm.REGISTRY).read_text()) if r["id"] == sid] \
        if (root / dshm.REGISTRY).exists() else []
    row = reg[-1] if reg else {}
    left = 0

    # 1. Simulator dshm-<ID> (each device with that name, by UDID).
    sim = row.get("sim") or f"dshm-{sid}"
    owner = Path(os.environ.get("DSHM_OWNERS", "/tmp/dshm-guard")) / sim   # the guard's record
    pid = owner.read_text().split()[0] if owner.is_file() and owner.read_text().split() else ""
    if pid.isdigit() and subprocess.run(["kill", "-0", pid], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: left simulator {sim}: a demo or review (pid {pid}) owns it")
        left += 1
    elif sim.startswith("dshm-"):
        for d in dshm.simulators():
            if d["name"] == sim:
                destroy(dry, f"simulator {sim} ({d['udid']})",
                        ["-", "xcrun", "simctl", "shutdown", d["udid"]],
                        ["xcrun", "simctl", "delete", d["udid"]])

    # 2. /tmp/dshm-<id> and /tmp/dshm-<id>-*. Not while a process uses them: the review of
    #    another slice can run this slice's demo (scripts/demo/<id>.sh) as a regression.
    key = sid.lower()
    ps = [l.strip() for l in subprocess.run(["ps", "-axo", "command="], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split("\n")
          if l.strip() and "scripts/plan" not in l]
    for path in dshm.slice_tmp_paths(sid):
        users = [l for l in ps if re.search(rf"{re.escape(path.name)}(?![\w.-])|scripts/demo/{key}\.sh", l)]
        if users:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left {path}: a process uses it ({users[0][:80]})")
            left += 1
        else:
            destroy(dry, str(path), ("rm", str(path)))

    # 3. Worktrees and branches of the slice, only when merged into <target> and clean.
    here = {str(root), str(dshm.main_checkout())}
    wts = dshm.worktree_entries(cwd=root)
    branches = dshm.slice_branches(sid, cwd=root)
    reg_branch = row.get("branch")
    if reg_branch and reg_branch not in branches and \
            dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"refs/heads/{reg_branch}", cwd=root, check=False):
        branches.append(reg_branch)

    def merged(commit):
        return subprocess.run(["git", "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", commit, target], cwd=root).returncode == 0

    for br in branches:
        tip = dshm.git("rev-parse", br, cwd=root)
        holders = [w for w in wts if w["branch"] == br and w["path"] not in here]
        if any(w["branch"] == br and w["path"] in here for w in wts):
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left branch {br}: it is checked out here")
            left += 1
            continue
        if not merged(tip):
            where = f" and worktree {holders[0]['path']}" if holders else ""
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left branch {br}{where}: {tip[:7]} is not merged into {target[:7]}")
            left += 1
            continue
        ok = True
        for w in holders:
            dirty = subprocess.run(["git", "--no-optional-locks", "-C", w["path"], "status", "--porcelain"],
                                   capture_output=True, text=True)
            if dirty.returncode != 0:
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left worktree {w['path']}: git status failed")
                ok = False
            elif dirty.stdout.strip():
                n = len(dirty.stdout.strip().split("\n"))
                print(f"plan: cleanup: left worktree {w['path']} ({br}): {n} uncommitted or untracked file(s)")
                ok = False
            elif not destroy(dry, f"worktree {w['path']} ({br})", ["git", "-C", str(root), "worktree", "remove", w["path"]]):
                ok = False
        if not ok:
            left += 1
            continue
        if not destroy(dry, f"branch {br}", ["git", "-C", str(root), "branch", "-d", br]):
            left += 1

    # 4. DSHM_HOME, only inside ~/.dshm/.
    home = row.get("home")
    if home:
        safe = dshm.safe_slice_home(home)
        if safe is None:
            print(f"plan: cleanup: left DSHM_HOME {home}: it is not inside ~/.dshm/")
            left += 1
        elif os.path.lexists(safe):
            destroy(dry, f"DSHM_HOME {safe}", ("rm", safe))

    if left:
        print(f"plan: cleanup: {left} thing(s) left; remove them by hand when they are not needed")
    return 0


def cmd_cleanup(p, a):
    need_main()
    if not p.exists:   # no plan: every slice of the last one is over; cleanup keeps its own checks
        return cleanup(p.root, a.id, dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "main^{commit}", cwd=p.root), cleanup_dry(a))
    _, r = p.row(a.id)
    if r["status"] not in ("review", "done"):
        raise PlanError(f"{a.id} is {r['status']} in §0; cleanup is only for a merged slice (review or done)")
    target = dshm.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "main^{commit}", cwd=p.root)
    return cleanup(p.root, a.id, target, cleanup_dry(a))


def cmd_tick(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    hits = [(i, m) for i, m in dshm.items(p.lines, a.id) if m.group("box") == " " and a.match in m.group("desc")]
    if not hits:
        raise PlanError(f"no open item of {a.id} contains {a.match!r}")
    if len(hits) > 1:
        raise PlanError(f"{len(hits)} open items of {a.id} contain {a.match!r}; give more of the text:\n" +
                        "\n".join("  " + p.lines[i][:120] for i, _ in hits))
    i, m = hits[0]
    if m.group("tier") == "human":
        raise PlanError("only the user ticks [human] items (WORKFLOW.md §12)")
    p.lines[i] = f"- [x] [{m.group('tier')}] {m.group('desc').strip()} — Evidence: {a.evidence.strip()}"
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN {a.id}: tick \"{m.group('desc').strip()[:50]}\"")


def cmd_slice_log(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    s, e = dshm.slice_bounds(p.lines, a.id)
    while e > s and p.lines[e - 1].strip() == "":
        e -= 1
    p.lines[e:e] = format_entry(a.title, read_body(a.body))
    return p.save(a, f"PLAN {a.id}: Log, {a.title.strip().rstrip('.')}")


def cmd_slice_status(p, a):
    need_slice_branch(a.id)
    if a.status not in dshm.STATUSES:
        raise PlanError(f"status must be one of {', '.join(dshm.STATUSES)}")
    s, e = dshm.slice_bounds(p.lines, a.id)
    for i in range(s, e):
        if p.lines[i].startswith("**Status** "):
            p.lines[i] = re.sub(r"^\*\*Status\*\* \S+", f"**Status** {a.status}", p.lines[i])
            return p.save(a, f"PLAN {a.id}: status {a.status}")
    raise PlanError(f"{a.id} has no **Status** line")


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="scripts/plan", description="Bookkeeping in PLAN.md (see the file header).")
    common = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    common.add_argument("--commit", action="store_true", help="commit the change")
    common.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="print the diff, change nothing")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    def add(name, fn, *args):
        sp = sub.add_parser(name, parents=[common])
        sp.set_defaults(fn=fn)
        return sp

    sp = add("show", cmd_show); sp.add_argument("id")
    sp = add("title", cmd_title); sp.add_argument("--milestone")
    add("lint", cmd_lint)
    sp = add("dag", cmd_dag); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp = add("passed", cmd_passed); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp.add_argument("--base", default="HEAD")
    sp = add("verify", cmd_verify); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--base", default="HEAD")
    sp = add("merge", cmd_merge); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--into", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--allow-changed-evidence", dest="allow", action="append", default=[], metavar="PATH")
    sp = add("new", cmd_new); sp.add_argument("title")
    sp = add("add", cmd_add); sp.add_argument("kind", choices=[*plangen.KINDS, "exit"]); sp.add_argument("name")
    sp.add_argument("--why", default=""); sp.add_argument("--cuts", default="")
    sp.add_argument("--demo", default=""); sp.add_argument("--not", dest="not_", default="")
    sp.add_argument("--done", action="append"); sp.add_argument("--needs")
    sp = add("row", cmd_row); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("status")
    sp.add_argument("--branch"); sp.add_argument("--next")
    sp = add("log", cmd_log); sp.add_argument("title"); sp.add_argument("--body")
    sp = add("fix", cmd_fix); sp.add_argument("name"); sp.add_argument("--bug", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--needs")
    sp = add("pending", cmd_pending); sp.add_argument("slice"); sp.add_argument("kind"); sp.add_argument("item")
    sp.add_argument("--branch", default="main"); sp.add_argument("--commit-ref")
    sp = add("assign", cmd_assign); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("--branch", required=True)
    sp.add_argument("--worktree"); sp.add_argument("--from", dest="from_commit")
    sp.add_argument("--decisions", type=int, default=dshm.DECISION_BLOCK); sp.add_argument("--note")
    sp = add("merged", cmd_merged); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("merge_commit", metavar="merge-commit"); sp.add_argument("--note")
    sp.add_argument("--keep", action="store_true", help="skip the cleanup")
    sp = add("cleanup", cmd_cleanup); sp.add_argument("id")
    sp = add("tick", cmd_tick); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("match")
    sp.add_argument("--evidence", required=True)
    sp = add("slice-log", cmd_slice_log); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("title"); sp.add_argument("--body")
    sp = add("slice-status", cmd_slice_status); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.add_argument("status")

    a = ap.parse_args()
    try:
        for attr in ("id",):
            if getattr(a, attr, None):
                dshm.check_id(getattr(a, attr))
        p = Plan(dshm.toplevel())
        if not p.exists and a.fn not in (cmd_new, cmd_cleanup, cmd_dag, cmd_passed, cmd_verify, cmd_merge):
            raise PlanError(plangen.NO_PLAN)
        return a.fn(p, a)
    except PlanError as e:
        print(f"plan: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
